counterfactuals.output:
A chip comprising:

a data input/output (I/O) interface configured to receive input data signals from, and transmit output data signals to, an external electronic system;

an input/output block coupled to the data I/O interface and configured to condition, buffer, serialize, deserialize, retime, encode, decode, or otherwise process electrical data signals communicated through the data I/O interface;

a signal processing block coupled to the input/output block and configured to perform digital or mixed-signal processing on the electrical data signals to generate one or more drive control signals;

a driver module coupled to the signal processing block and configured to generate one or more driver output signals based at least in part on the one or more drive control signals; and

a driver interface coupled to the driver module and configured to electrically connect the driver module to a silicon photonics device,

wherein the driver interface is arranged to provide the one or more driver output signals to the silicon photonics device to control at least one optical component of the silicon photonics device.
